   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the domestic relations law, in relation to designating lay\nindividuals to solemnize marriages; and to repeal certain provisions of the\nexecutive law related thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S2234",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2234-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§11, 12, 13 & 13-b, add §11-d, Dom Rel L; rpld §110, Exec L (as proposed in S.739-A & A.6300-A)",
    "lawSection": "Domestic Relations Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2234\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN-SIGAL\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the domestic relations law, in relation to designating\nlay individuals to solemnize marriages; and to repeal certain provisions\nof the executive law related thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to L.2022, ch.798, to modify the process by\nwhich a layperson applies for a one-day marriage officiant license.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends multiple provisions of L2022, ch.798. Under the\nunderlying chapter, a layperson applied to the Secretary of State for a\none-day marriage officiant license. Under this chapter amendment, a\nlayperson applies to a town or city clerk for a license.\n\nSection 1 through 4 amend the Domestic Relations Law to replace refer-\nences to the Secretary of State with \"town or city clerk's).\"\n\nSection 5 repeals section 110 of the Executive Law, which under the\nunderlying chapter authorized the Secretary of State to issue one-day\nmarriage officiant licenses.\n\nSection 6 adds a new section to the Domestic Relations Law that author-\nizes town and city clerks to issue one-day marriage officiant licenses.\n\nSection 7 is the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 789 of the Laws of 2022. S.739-A passed the\nSenate in March 2022, and A.6300-A passed the Assembly in June 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the Laws of 2022 amending the Domestic Relations Law and the\nExecutive Law relating to designating lay individuals to solemnize\nmarriages, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.  739-A and A.\n6300-A, takes effect.\n",
